What is process?
A process is a program that is currently running on your computer.

Think about your Windows computer:
- Chrome running = process.
- VS Code running = process.
- Music player running = process.
Linux works the same way.

Every process has a unique identification number called a PID (Process ID).
For example:
sleep 100
This starts a process that waits for 100 seconds.
ps Displays processes
ps aux - Displays detailed process information
top - Live process monitoring
htop - nteractive process monitoring
pgrep - Finds process IDs by name
kill PID - Sends a signal to a process
kill -9 PID - Forcefully terminates a process
jobs - Lists background jobs in your shell
&	Runs a command in the background

what is service?
A service is a program that usually runs in the background and provides functionality to the system or other applications.

Process = a running program.
Service = a program managed to provide a background function.
systemctl is used to manage services on Linux systems using systemd.
sudo systemctl start nginx	Starts Nginx
sudo systemctl stop nginx	Stops Nginx
sudo systemctl restart nginx	Restarts Nginx
sudo systemctl status nginx	Checks Nginx status
sudo systemctl enable nginx	Enables automatic startup
sudo systemctl disable nginx	Disables automatic startup

